# Allowlist, not a denylist. This directory is a live ComfyUI Portable install: models alone are
# ~600 GiB, plus python_embeded, venvs, user data and an upstream ComfyUI checkout that has its
# own .git. A denylist that misses one entry tries to commit a 42 GiB safetensors, so everything
# is ignored by default and tracked paths are re-included one by one below.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/tools/
!/custom_nodes/
!/*.md
!/inspect_quant.py
!/_check_accel.py

# The per-layer measurements themselves, and only those. A `.analysis.json` is ~60 KiB and is the
# expensive part of this project to reproduce -- it costs a calibration run on a GPU that is
# shared with another session. The `.calib.pt` files beside them are the raw activation samples,
# 170-384 MiB each and 2.2 GiB in total, and they are an input to the analysis rather than a
# result: kept out.
!/calib/
/calib/*
!/calib/*.analysis.json

# Generated by tools/quant_audit.py from whatever is on disk, so it describes this machine rather
# than the code. Regenerable in one command.
/quantization_inventory.json
/quantization_inventory.md

# Nothing but source in the tracked trees. Written generically on purpose: the first version
# of this named tools/ only, and __pycache__ from custom_nodes/ went straight into a commit.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
tools/calib/
tools/bench/

bench/quality_ladder/*.png
